  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "\\(R\\) varies directly as \\(S\\) and inversely as \\(T.\\) When \\(R=\\dfrac43\\) and \\(T=\\dfrac9{14},\\) \\(S=\\dfrac37.\\) Find \\(S\\) when \\(R=\\sqrt{48}\\) and \\(T=\\sqrt{75}.\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(28\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(30\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(40\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(42\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(60\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "30"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1962-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because \\(R=\\frac{kS}{T},\\) we have \\(S=\\frac{RT}{k}.\\) Hence \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\frac{S_2}{S_1} &=\\frac{R_2T_2}{R_1T_1}\\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{48}\\sqrt{75}} {(\\frac{4}{3})(\\frac{9}{14})}\\\\ &=\\frac{60}{\\frac{6}{7}}=70. \\end{aligned} \\] Therefore \\(S_2=(\\frac{3}{7})\\cdot70=30.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Write the variation as \\(R=\\frac{kS}{T}\\)",
        "For fixed \\(k,\\) the quantity \\(\\frac{RT}{S}\\) is constant"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
